<article class="env-proposition" id="8E78DB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8E78DB">Proposition <span data-tag="8E78DB">8.2.4.4</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a model category, and let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &amp;  A \ar [dl]^{i} \ar [dr]^{j} &amp;  \\ A_0 \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  A_1 \ar [dl] \\ &amp;  A_0 \coprod _ A A_1 }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a pushout square in $\calC $. This diagram is also a homotopy pushout square if either of the following conditions is satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
The objects $A$ and $A_0$ are cofibrant, and $j$ is a cofibration. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
The map $j$ is a cofibration, and $\calC $ is left proper. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>